==Important events==
{{spoilers}}
* {{adv|Silver}} obtains {{TP|Silver|Rhyperior}}.
* {{adv|Crystal}} encounters {{adv|Arceus}}, and makes an attempt to capture it.
* Silver gathers all sixteen [[plate]]s.
* {{adv|Gold}}, Silver, and Crystal enter the [[Sinjoh Ruins]].
* [[Petrel]] reveals he knows that Silver is Giovanni's son.
* Arceus creates {{p|Dialga}}, {{p|Palkia}}, and {{p|Giratina}}.

===VIZ edition only===
* [[Lance]], [[Pryce]], and {{adv|Giovanni}} battle and defeat the [[Pokémon of myth]].
* Pryce was chosen by {{adv|Celebi}} to exit the [[Ilex Forest]] Shrine and participate in the battle.
* {{adv|Gold}} battles {{adv|Arceus}} alone.
* Gold's {{p|Togepi}} evolves into {{p|Togetic}}, and then {{p|Togekiss}}.
* Togepi's [[Evolution]] calms Arceus's anger, because his [[friendship]] with Gold restores Arceus's faith in humans.
* [[Petrel]] had defeated [[Lance]] by disguising himself as {{adv|Yellow}}.
* [[Radio Director|Hiro]] reveals his plans on making [[Proteam Omega|an anime series]]. {{adv|Silver}} becomes interested in Proteam Omega.
* [[Cynthia]] meets [[Palmer]], and he reveals that a [[Reg|Regigigas]] is in his possession.

==Party changes==
===Additions===
*Silver's {{TP|Silver|Rhyperior}} prior to [[PS449]].

===Evolutions===
* Gold's {{p|Togepi}} "[[Togebo]]" evolves into {{p|Togetic}} in [[PS459]].
* Gold's {{p|Togetic}} "Togebo" evolves into {{p|Togekiss}} in [[PS459]].

==Trivia==
===Localization===
The [[VIZ Media]] release of this volume also includes the first four chapters from {{PAV|43}}. This is because [[PS460]] is the final chapter of the {{MangaArc|HeartGold & SoulSilver}} and VIZ Media was already publishing the {{MangaArc|Black & White}} as a separately numbered series. A similar split was done with {{PAV|14}} and {{PAV|15}}, where the last chapter of the {{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}} was moved from the beginning of Volume 15 to the end of Volume 14.

